<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Cicero</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1455">1455</a>–<a href="/years/1499">1499</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as John Cicero, Elector of Brandenburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cicero">Cicero</a> was Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> from 1486 to 1499, son of Albert <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achilles">Achilles</a>. He was the first elector to reside permanently in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>, making it the capital of the Mark, and he introduced an excise on beer. His nickname, 'Cicero', referred to his reputed eloquence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-cicero.jpg" alt="John Cicero" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JohannCicero1500.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
